WEBVTT

00:00:05.179 --> 00:00:10.429
<v Callum Reid>Morning all. Tuesday third, quick stand-up and then I'll let you crack on. Everyone alright?</v>

00:00:11.359 --> 00:00:16.260
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, not bad. Bit grim out there though, isn't it. Proper sideways rain again.</v>

00:00:18.489 --> 00:00:19.690
<v Hannah Price>Standard February.</v>

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:23.929
<v Jamie Brennan>I got soaked just from car park to door.</v>

00:00:24.789 --> 00:00:32.840
<v Sarah Okafor>Mm. Weekend's meant to be a bit brighter though, so if it holds I might actually get out in the garden for once.</v>

00:00:34.189 --> 00:00:35.390
<v Grace Liu>Brave.</v>

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:39.119
<v Fiona Doyle>You'll need waders, not gardening gloves.</v>

00:00:40.229 --> 00:00:43.380
<v Callum Reid>Right, before we become the Met Office. Sarah, nights?</v>

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:55.719
<v Sarah Okafor>Quiet enough overall. Just an observation really, noticed the line 3 screw was running a bit warm on nights but it settled down, so nothing for today off the back of that.</v>

00:00:56.310 --> 00:01:01.560
<v Callum Reid>Okay, noted. Keep an eye on it, but yeah, not a job from this meeting.</v>

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:04.219
<v Callum Reid>Han, you next.</v>

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:14.450
<v Hannah Price>Er, quality-wise all fine on the morning samples. And before I forget, that football last night was awful. Well, unless you support them, I suppose.</v>

00:01:15.829 --> 00:01:18.629
<v Jamie Brennan>Oh it was brilliant, what you on about?</v>

00:01:20.629 --> 00:01:24.129
<v Hannah Price>Rubbish. They were hanging on for dear life second half.</v>

00:01:25.730 --> 00:01:29.230
<v Priya Raman>Can we not do VAR at eight in the morning?</v>

00:01:30.430 --> 00:01:32.530
<v Callum Reid>Please, spare me. Anything real, Han?</v>

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:43.680
<v Hannah Price>Yeah. Blocker on the GT1 fuel valve still, still waiting on parts for the GT1 fuel valve, nothing we can do until they arrive, so that's not moving today.</v>

00:01:45.329 --> 00:01:48.480
<v Callum Reid>Yep, parked till stores gets something through. Anything else?</v>

00:01:49.519 --> 00:01:55.469
<v Hannah Price>I can run a function test on the boiler safety valve. I'll do that first thing tomorrow.</v>

00:01:57.489 --> 00:01:59.239
<v Callum Reid>Good. Get that booked in.</v>

00:02:01.290 --> 00:02:02.489
<v Hannah Price>Will do.</v>

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:04.599
<v Callum Reid>Jamie?</v>

00:02:05.719 --> 00:02:11.669
<v Jamie Brennan>Yesterday, I tested the booster pump yesterday and it's all fine now, so that's done and gone.</v>

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:13.469
<v Callum Reid>Nice one.</v>

00:02:14.719 --> 00:02:18.219
<v Jamie Brennan>Procurement side, couple of deliveries due before lunch. Nothing dramatic.</v>

00:02:20.069 --> 00:02:32.319
<v Callum Reid>I need you on something though, Jamie Brennan — sort the permit to work and isolation for the turbine two water valve. That one's safety critical, straight away. I need it ready tomorrow at 9:30.</v>

00:02:33.949 --> 00:02:42.699
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, okay. I'll sort the permit to work and isolation for the turbine two water valve, tomorrow at 9:30. I'll get on that straight away.</v>

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:54.210
<v Callum Reid>Cheers. And second one, Jamie — can you go to Tollgate Water Treatment Works to pick up the replacement parts for the Line 1 Hydraulic Power Unit this afternoon?</v>

00:02:54.599 --> 00:03:04.050
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, I can do that. I'll go to Tollgate Water Treatment Works to pick up the replacement parts for the Line 1 Hydraulic Power Unit this afternoon.</v>

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:06.979
<v Callum Reid>Spot on.</v>

00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:10.060
<v Callum Reid>Priya?</v>

00:03:11.819 --> 00:03:21.969
<v Priya Raman>Nothing major from me. Panels all behaving. I still want a look at that nuisance trip on line two when we get chance, but not today, no immediate action.</v>

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:25.569
<v Callum Reid>Fine.</v>

00:03:27.289 --> 00:03:28.490
<v Callum Reid>Grace?</v>

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:44.389
<v Grace Liu>Two from me. The water booster's been a bit noisy on and off, not enough to panic about but it needs doing this week — I'll take vibration readings on the water booster by the end of the week.</v>

00:03:46.210 --> 00:03:47.409
<v Callum Reid>Yep.</v>

00:03:49.439 --> 00:03:58.889
<v Grace Liu>And also, because of the planned job there, it needs doing this week, I'll update the risk assessment for work on the main isolation valve this morning.</v>

00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:00.439
<v Callum Reid>Good, thanks Grace.</v>

00:04:02.699 --> 00:04:03.900
<v Callum Reid>Fi?</v>

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:11.620
<v Fiona Doyle>Scheduling-wise, just so you know, I signed off the inspection on the GT2 bearing on Tuesday, so that's already complete.</v>

00:04:12.129 --> 00:04:13.330
<v Callum Reid>Good.</v>

00:04:15.069 --> 00:04:22.069
<v Fiona Doyle>And blocker-wise, can't get to the line 3 barrel until production gives us a window, so that's stuck for now.</v>

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:28.060
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, not today on that, we've got no gap till at least late shift.</v>

00:04:30.350 --> 00:04:33.500
<v Callum Reid>Right, leave line 3 barrel where it is then.</v>

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:42.699
<v Callum Reid>One small one on utilities: swap the filter on the air dryer. It's low priority, first thing tomorrow. Han, can you pick that up?</v>

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:52.019
<v Hannah Price>Uh, not really. I've got the boiler safety valve first thing tomorrow and then audits stacked after that. I won't get near it.</v>

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:55.430
<v Callum Reid>Fair. Fi, can you take it instead?</v>

00:04:56.709 --> 00:05:04.410
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, alright. I'll swap the filter on the air dryer first thing tomorrow. Low priority, so if nothing falls over before then.</v>

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:09.050
<v Callum Reid>That's fine, as long as it's done.</v>

00:05:10.509 --> 00:05:11.709
<v Fiona Doyle>Yep.</v>

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:16.509
<v Callum Reid>Anything else knocking about that actually needs agreeing today?</v>

00:05:17.439 --> 00:05:24.439
<v Sarah Okafor>No, that's me. Just the weather, again. If it snows on top of this lot I'm working from my bed.</v>

00:05:26.610 --> 00:05:28.009
<v Jamie Brennan>Production supervisor'll love that.</v>

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:30.060
<v Callum Reid>Absolutely not.</v>

00:05:31.519 --> 00:05:34.319
<v Hannah Price>He says that, but he'd do the same.</v>

00:05:36.569 --> 00:05:37.769
<v Callum Reid>I would not.</v>

00:05:38.410 --> 00:05:40.860
<v Priya Raman>Mic off, camera off, "sorry bad connection".</v>

00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:46.019
<v Callum Reid>Cheek. Right, recapping so nobody wriggles out of it.</v>

00:05:48.089 --> 00:05:52.639
<v Callum Reid>Han's got the function test on the boiler safety valve first thing tomorrow.</v>

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:56.069
<v Hannah Price>Yep.</v>

00:05:56.930 --> 00:06:07.079
<v Callum Reid>Grace is taking vibration readings on the water booster by the end of the week, and updating the risk assessment for work on the main isolation valve this morning.</v>

00:06:07.399 --> 00:06:08.600
<v Grace Liu>Correct.</v>

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:20.800
<v Callum Reid>Jamie Brennan is sorting the permit to work and isolation for the turbine two water valve — that one's safety critical, straight away — for tomorrow at 9:30.</v>

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:23.560
<v Jamie Brennan>Yep, on it.</v>

00:06:25.149 --> 00:06:33.199
<v Callum Reid>And Jamie's going to Tollgate Water Treatment Works to pick up the replacement parts for the Line 1 Hydraulic Power Unit this afternoon.</v>

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:36.189
<v Jamie Brennan>That's me, yeah.</v>

00:06:37.490 --> 00:06:42.040
<v Callum Reid>Fi's swapping the filter on the air dryer first thing tomorrow, low priority.</v>

00:06:42.579 --> 00:06:43.779
<v Fiona Doyle>Yep.</v>

00:06:46.199 --> 00:06:56.699
<v Callum Reid>Blocked stuff stays blocked: GT1 fuel valve waiting on parts, line 3 barrel waiting on a production window. Done stuff stays done: booster pump tested, GT2 bearing inspection signed off.</v>

00:06:58.269 --> 00:07:03.519
<v Sarah Okafor>And line 3 screw was just a watch item on nights, not a fresh job.</v>

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:07.430
<v Callum Reid>Exactly that. Anything urgent before we break?</v>

00:07:08.050 --> 00:07:09.250
<v Priya Raman>Nope.</v>

00:07:10.120 --> 00:07:11.319
<v Grace Liu>All good.</v>

00:07:11.850 --> 00:07:13.050
<v Hannah Price>Fine by me.</v>

00:07:14.829 --> 00:07:16.029
<v Fiona Doyle>Yep.</v>

00:07:17.720 --> 00:07:18.920
<v Jamie Brennan>All set.</v>

00:07:20.230 --> 00:07:21.430
<v Callum Reid>Right, thanks all.</v>
